From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 18:01:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dismount a riding target before teleporting it, like Paper

Entity#teleportAsync refuses outright when the target is a passenger, and
CraftEntity#teleportAsync always passes TELEPORT_FLAG_TELEPORT_PASSENGERS, so
every Bukkit API teleport of a rider returns false and does nothing - boats,
minecarts, horses, seats, mounts. 25 teleport(...)Z callsites across 9 delivery
jars, 15 of which discard the return value and cannot even notice.

Paper's semantic, measured with the same probe on both platforms rather than
assumed: teleporting a passenger dismounts that passenger and moves it, leaving
the vehicle and any other passengers alone. Cancellation already matches. This
restores only that single-target semantic, at the API boundary, on the thread
that owns the entity.

Deliberately not included: the flag's meaning is untouched and no assumption is
made that its condition is inverted; vehicle trees are not moved. A teleported
vehicle dropping its passengers here where Paper keeps them mounted is a
separate divergence, recorded rather than fixed alongside this.

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftEntity.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftEntity.java
index 4fec4bd78ddcf23714fd705635452930af806c1f..b10a72af64aff0bb3683854ab6fb841874f786c4 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftEntity.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftEntity.java
@@ -1175,6 +1175,11 @@ public abstract class CraftEntity implements org.bukkit.entity.Entity {
         // Folia start - region threading
         java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture<Boolean> ret = new java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture<>();
         java.util.function.Consumer<Entity> run = (Entity nmsEntity) -> {
+            // Lecithin - Paper dismounts a riding target before teleporting it; the platform refuses
+            // outright instead. Restores that one semantic here, on the owning thread, and leaves the
+            // vehicle and any other passengers alone. See LecithinRidingTeleport for the measured
+            // Paper baseline this follows.
+            final Entity lecithinVehicle = fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinRidingTeleport.dismountForTeleport(nmsEntity);
             boolean success = nmsEntity.teleportAsync(
                 ((CraftWorld)locationClone.getWorld()).getHandle(),
                 new net.minecraft.world.phys.Vec3(locationClone.getX(), locationClone.getY(), locationClone.getZ()),
@@ -1186,6 +1191,10 @@ public abstract class CraftEntity implements org.bukkit.entity.Entity {
                 }
             );
             if (!success) {
+                // Lecithin - the refusal may be a handler cancelling the event, which the platform
+                // decides after the dismount above. Paper leaves a cancelled target mounted, so put
+                // it back rather than leaving a half-broken passenger graph.
+                fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinRidingTeleport.restoreMount(nmsEntity, lecithinVehicle);
                 ret.complete(Boolean.FALSE);
             }
         };
